; The last mark: one mark from the game, bid 42, not 84. Winning 42 (S-0170-a, its
; second half; S-0082-a, an 84 is two marks). Cluster B of docs/cross-game.md.
;
; Both contracts need every point, so the make is the same event under each; only
; the stake differs. Made, either wins the match. Set, the setters gain one mark
; under the 42 and two under the 84. So from every state where the bidder's side
; needs one mark, for every outcome of the hand, the 42 leaves a state at least as
; good under every match-win value: no deal, belief or field enters. Exact.
(dominates last-mark
  (contracts (marks 1) (marks 2))
  (frame (scoring marks 7) (short 1))
  (utility match-win))
